WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.615
"Come and get it!" called Cookie.

2
00:00:04.616 --> 00:00:09.576
Frank and the other cowboys came up to Cookie’s wagon.

3
00:00:09.577 --> 00:00:16.841
The children served the hungry men and everyone sat around a big fire to eat.

4
00:00:16.842 --> 00:00:21.928
"Frank says you can stay," Cookie said to Vinnie and Mandy.

5
00:00:21.929 --> 00:00:25.249
"But you’d better keep out of trouble."

6
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:29.972
"We promise!" exclaimed the children.

7
00:00:29.973 --> 00:00:35.058
Mandy listened to the cowboys tell stories, and said,

8
00:00:35.059 --> 00:00:39.293
"I wish I had a cowboy hat and boots."

9
00:00:39.294 --> 00:00:43.880
"I wish I had a gun!" Vinnie cried.

10
00:00:43.881 --> 00:00:48.058
"Hey, kids," a cowboy called out.

11
00:00:48.059 --> 00:00:50.961
He held up a harmonica.

12
00:00:50.962 --> 00:00:53.282
"Sing something."

13
00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:57.653
"I can’t sing," said Vinnie shyly.

14
00:00:57.654 --> 00:01:03.608
"He’s right! He can’t sing!" giggled Mandy.

15
00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:07.178
"Come on," the cowboy said.

16
00:01:07.179 --> 00:01:11.401
"Singing calms the cattle, so they can sleep."

17
00:01:11.402 --> 00:01:15.028
"Like a lullaby?" asked Vinnie.

18
00:01:15.029 --> 00:01:18.849
"Yep. We all sing, so don’t be shy,"

19
00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:23.695
said the cowboy, and he began to play."Oh,

20
00:01:23.696 --> 00:01:29.518
give me a home where the buffalo roam," sang

21
00:01:29.519 --> 00:01:34.394
Vinnie as the cattle mooed happily. Meanwhile,

22
00:01:34.395 --> 00:01:38.811
Mandy was helping Cookie clean up. "What

23
00:01:38.812 --> 00:01:42.908
is the Chisholm Trail?" she asked. "Well,

24
00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:47.986
we take the cattle from Texas along the trail to Kansas. The

25
00:01:47.987 --> 00:01:54.073
cattle end up at the market where they are sold," explained Cookie. "How

26
00:01:54.074 --> 00:01:58.138
long does it take?" asked Mandy. "Depends

27
00:01:58.139 --> 00:02:02.526
on the weather and the Indians," said Cookie. "It

28
00:02:02.527 --> 00:02:06.001
can take from two to three months." Later

29
00:02:06.002 --> 00:02:12.039
some cowboys unrolled their beds and went to sleep.

30
00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:20.580
Others just leaned back, covered their eyes with their hats, and slept on the ground.

31
00:02:20.581 --> 00:02:25.844
Cookie gave Mandy and Vinnie bedrolls. Vinnie yawned.

32
00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:30.936
A few men were walking around, staring at the herd.

33
00:02:30.937 --> 00:02:35.532
"Why aren’t those men sleeping?" Vinnie asked Frank.

34
00:02:35.533 --> 00:02:39.683
"They’re guarding the cattle," Frank replied.

35
00:02:39.684 --> 00:02:42.835
"From what?" asked Mandy.

36
00:02:42.836 --> 00:02:48.333
"Wild animals, cattle thieves, and Indians," said Frank.

37
00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:52.105
The children heard howling in the distance.

38
00:02:52.106 --> 00:02:55.569
Mandy moved closer to her brother.

39
00:02:55.570 --> 00:03:00.845
The next morning, the children woke to a sunny day.

40
00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:04.743
Everyone was already up and ready to go.

41
00:03:04.744 --> 00:03:10.749
The wagon was loaded, and the cattle were starting to move again.

42
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:14.391
"Good morning, kids," Cookie called.

43
00:03:14.392 --> 00:03:19.538
"You missed breakfast, but I saved you some biscuits.

44
00:03:19.539 --> 00:03:21.598
We have to get going."

45
00:03:21.599 --> 00:03:26.071
"Where?" asked Vinnie, munching on his biscuit.

46
00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:29.008
"It’s time to get back on the trail,"

47
00:03:29.009 --> 00:03:34.379
said Frank as he brought over Vinnie’s horse from the previous day.

48
00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.500
The horse sniffed Vinnie’s biscuit.

49
00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:40.855
"You come with me."

50
00:03:40.856 --> 00:03:45.012
"And Mandy can ride with me," said Cookie.

51
00:03:45.013 --> 00:03:49.436
He picked her up and helped her climb onto the wagon seat.

52
00:03:49.437 --> 00:03:53.694
The horses followed the cattle at an easy pace.

53
00:03:53.695 --> 00:03:58.271
They rode over dry, flat prairies of tall grass.

54
00:03:58.272 --> 00:04:03.149
The sun was hot, and the sky was bright blue.

55
00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.814
There was a soft wind.

56
00:04:05.815 --> 00:04:10.983
Vinnie wiped his face with his sleeve and thought:

57
00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:17.521
"This is the life of a cowboy!"

